course: dictionary
lesson: 2310
title: Nouns that name a thing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A noun names a thing, a person or a place. A crocus is a noun: it names a small flower that comes up early in spring. When you meet a word like this, ask what it names and what the words around it tell you. «Spices come from every part of a plant» tells you that a crocus is a plant.
explain: The sentence gives another clue: saffron is «the red threads in a crocus flower». So a crocus flower has red threads inside, and those threads are used to make a spice. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: A noun can change its ending to show more than one. One crocus, two crocuses. Your dictionary also lists croci, another plural, so check there if you are unsure.
fact: A crocus is a small flower that comes up early in spring, often purple, yellow or white, and shaped like a cup.
fact: A crocus grows from a bulb-like corm, which stores food underground.
fact: Crocuses can come up even through snow, so they are a sign that spring is on its way.
fact: Some crocuses flower in autumn, and their red threads give saffron, a spice.
fact: «Saffron» means a spice made from the red threads of a crocus.
exercise: «Spices come from every part of a plant: pepper is a berry, saffron is the red threads in a crocus flower, and cinnamon is curled-up tree bark.» What is saffron? | A kind of tree bark | A berry from a pepper plant | A flower that comes up in spring | *The red threads in a crocus flower
exercise: What is a crocus? | A large tree that grows in forests | A bird that visits in winter | *A small flower that comes up early in spring | A spice made from tree bark
exercise: Which is a correct plural of crocus? | Crocusies | Crocuse | Crocuss | *Crocuses
test: Why are crocuses a sign of spring? | They lose their petals in winter | *They come up early in spring, even through snow | They are always red | They grow only in autumn
test: What do crocuses often stand for in poems and art? | Dark nights | *New beginnings | Winter sleep | Bad weather
exam: Which is true of a crocus? | It is a bird that flies south | It grows only in deserts | *It grows from a bulb-like corm and comes up in spring | It is a spice
